Version 0.4.0 (in progress):
    * Architecture following "Architecture logicielle Robotik" (2026-10-11):
      - plugins/<Name>/{plugin.yaml, src, worlds, scenarios, experiments,
        data}; manifest v2: api_version checked before dlopen, runtime asset
        packs and plugin dependencies checked before setup
      - versioned asset packs (data/packs/<id>/pack.yaml, SPDX license),
        models named robotik.tools.vacuum, no lookup relative to the
        current directory
      - world files: robot, tools keeping their identity and actuators,
        simulated bodies (free/fixed URDF, free boxes), props, attachments
        to a frame of another entity
      - scenario files: world, controller, trajectories, faults, timeout,
        stop_when, assertions; oracle perception only when asked
      - assertion engine: always, end, at, within, eventually, sequence;
        verdicts keep the measured value, the bound and the time; world
        queries (pose_error, on, inside, collision_count...)
      - experiments: cases, seeds, overrides, injected faults, common
        evaluation; headless runner with a JSON report
      - sensors: Measurement header, NoiseModel (bias, noise, resolution,
        saturation), latency, every sensor type in YAML
      - trajectories in their own files, in the frame of a world entity
      - reinforcement learning: named and bounded spaces (privileged
        dimensions flagged), SimulationEnvironment from an observation
        builder, an action adapter and a reward evaluator, episode ends
        (success, failure, time limit, aborted), JSON episode log
    * Painter: the easel and the canvas are world entities; the scenario
      proves the easel did not move
    * PickAndPlaceRL: one observation/action/reward shared by the pool and
      the simulator plugin; the observation reads the robot's beliefs
    * Headless: runs of a plugin that owns the clock end on the simulated
      time summed across episodes
    * Build: binaries relink when a static archive changes; the recorded
      git commit follows HEAD

Version 0.3.0:
    * Architecture following ARCHI.md:
      - compact robot API: Robot/RobotSession, SoA JointSet in SI units,
        sensors, actuators and RobotBackend (MuJoCo, kinematic, hardware)
      - every sensor and actuator is a resource; failures make it unavailable
      - SkillScheduler: resources, priorities, preemption, cancellation,
        preconditions and trace; behavior tree actions request skills
      - perception: Camera/FrameSource, PerceptionPipeline of Detectors,
        WorldModel with gating, landmark localization
      - seed hierarchy: replayable worlds, faults and sensor noise
      - scenario YAML: sensors, actuators, randomized objects, faults
      - EnvironmentPool for parallel and deterministic reinforcement learning
      - no OpenCV nor rendering in the library (SceneView hooks)
    * Simulator: rendered wrist camera, color detector, resources/faults
      panel, skill timeline with reasons, emergency stop, seed replay
    * Demos: LineFollower (AprilTag localization, OpenCV line tracking) and
      PickAndPlaceRL

Version 0.2.0:
    * Initial refactor:
      - using personal OpenGL renderer as third party managing USRD/STL and kinematic chain
      - using personal behavior tree as third party
      - using Pinnochio and Mujoco as third parties for IK and phyical engine
      - using behavior tree and robot skills
      - introduce scenario file: constructing the world and assertions on robot/world states
      - Standalone with pick and place demo using camera attached to the robot
      - not integrated: teach pendant and trajectory, behavior tree editor
      - evolution: compact display of behavior tree with color and timelines of skills

Version 0.1.0:
